# ── frontend deployment artifacts (F3-PROD-004-R3) ───────────────────────
# scripts/noramedi-frontend-deploy.sh runs INSIDE the production checkout and
# creates these names at the deployment root: dist.next (staging build),
# dist.next.stale-<UTC> (--clean-staging), dist.rollback-<tag>-<UTC> (the
# preserved bundle every deploy and rollback leaves behind, deliberately never
# deleted), and the state file that makes rollback deterministic.
#
# That script's own gate refuses to deploy from a non-empty
# `git status --porcelain`. Without these four rules a SUCCESSFUL deploy dirties
# its own checkout and blocks the next one — which is the self-blocking defect
# F3-PROD-004-R3 fixes. Ignoring them removes nothing from that gate: a modified
# tracked file or any other untracked path still fails it closed, and a stale
# staging directory is still refused by the script's own staging precondition,
# which is a filesystem check and not a git one.
#
# These are exact artifact names, not a wildcard over build output. `dist/`
# above does NOT cover `dist.next`: a .gitignore pattern matches whole path
# components, so "dist" never matches "dist.next" — it needs its own line.
dist.next/
dist.next.stale-*/
dist.rollback-*/
.noramedi-frontend-release-state
